# What the diff-reviewer platform itself may do on GitHub, as Christian: list and read the pull
# requests of the repositories it reviews, and post reviews of them. It is not an orchestra task:
# its token is issued by hand and held by the platform process, which sends
# `Authorization: Bearer kleis` to api.github.com through this proxy.
#
# Which reviews: for a repository in `direct` mode the platform posts a job's submission at once,
# as COMMENT only; APPROVE and REQUEST_CHANGES it posts only when a person clicks Post. kleis
# allows every review event, because it cannot tell the second request from the first: that rule
# is enforced by the platform, not here.
#
# `read` is every GET and HEAD under a listed repository's /repos/{owner}/{name}/…: contents,
# commits, issues, workflow runs, whatever the token can read there, not only pull requests.
#
# The repositories are the one list below, kept by the operator. Every request must name one of
# them: one about any other repository is refused, and so is one about none (`/user`, `/search`,
# `/rate_limit`, GraphQL), which would reach the rest of what the token can see. Editing the list
# takes effect for the token already issued, at the daemon's next reload.
#
# Written in datalog rather than `allow`: the GitHub extension's group `read` shadows the operation
# of that name, and the group would bring `api_read` and GraphQL with it. The operations are the
# REST API's `read` on a repository (pull requests, their details, their diffs), `review_pr` and
# `review_comment`; not cloning or fetching.
spec diff-reviewer-poster
  description "The diff-reviewer platform: reads the pull requests it reviews and posts approved reviews."
  max_ttl 90d

  account github/chrisflav
    datalog '''
      reviewed(["chrisflav/kleis"]);
      allowed($op) <- operation($op), ["read", "review_pr", "review_comment"].contains($op),
        repository($o, $r), reviewed($s), $s.contains($o + "/" + $r);
      check if allowed($x);
      reject if repository($o, $r), reviewed($s), !$s.contains($o + "/" + $r);
    '''
